-- title:
--   Residue of t df/f equals ordᵥ f
-- statement:
--   Let $K$ be a perfect field and $F$ a field equipped with a $K$-algebra structure, and suppose there is an element $x \in F$ such that $F$ is finite-dimensional over the intermediate field $K(x)$ generated by $x$. Let $v$ be a place of $F$ over $K$, that is, a valuation subring of $F$ that contains the image of $K$ under the structure map, is not all of $F$, and is a principal ideal ring; write $\operatorname{ord}_v$ for the associated integer-valued order function, defined as minus the logarithm of the adic valuation attached to the height-one prime of that ring. Let $t \in F$ satisfy $\operatorname{ord}_v t = 1$, and let $f \in F$ be nonzero. Let $\operatorname{diffCoeff} t (\mathrm{D}_{K/F} f)$ denote the coefficient attached to $\mathrm{d}f$ relative to $\mathrm{d}t$: a choice of $g \in F$ with $\mathrm{d}f = g \cdot \mathrm{d}t$ in $\Omega_{F/K}$ when such $g$ exists, and $0$ otherwise. The conclusion is twofold: first, the element $t \cdot \operatorname{diffCoeff} t (\mathrm{D}_{K/F} f) / f$ lies in the valuation subring of $v$; second, its value at $v$ — its image in the residue field, transported back to $K$ along a left inverse of the map $K \to$ residue field — equals the image in $K$ of the integer $\operatorname{ord}_v f$.
--
--   This is the residue formula for the logarithmic differential $\mathrm{d}f/f$ at a place of a function field in one variable: the regular function $t\,f'/f$ takes the value $\operatorname{ord}_v(f)\cdot 1_K$ at $v$, with no tameness hypothesis needed for the value. It is used for the statement that $f^{-1}\,\mathrm{d}f$ has at most a simple pole with logarithmic residue $\operatorname{ord}_v f$, and in the analysis of the geometric $j$-function on modular curves.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_AlgebraicCurve_Place_mul_diffCoeff_D_div_mem_and_evalAt_eq_intCast_ord.lean

